

# <type>: <what this commit does, imperative, max 72 chars, no period>
#
# - <what changed, and why if it is not obvious>
# - <optional second point>
# - <optional third point>
#
#
# Rules
# - type: feat | fix | test | docs | chore
# - Title says what the commit does to the code: "add", "reject", "store",
#   not "added" or "adding". Read it as "This commit will <title>".
# - 1 to 3 bullets, one line each, wrapped at 72 chars. Say why, not how.
# - At most 150 changed lines per commit, excluding package-lock.json.
# Lines starting with # are ignored.
